### Scenario 35 — Orchestrated saga happy path + admin inspection
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax.
### Prereq: run 00-smoke.http section 0 first (or have landlord/tenant/admin seeded).
###
### What this exercises:
###   1. Saga starts on support-decision and gets a sagaId.
###   2. PENALTY_APPLIED → penaltyCount++ → PENALTY_COUNTED → saga COMPLETED.
###   3. Admin reads /api/sagas/{id} and /api/claims/{id}/saga.
###
### Compensation arc (saga → COMPENSATING_REVOKE → COMPENSATED) is exercised
### indirectly: bring penalty-service or auth-service down between requests 35.6
### and 35.7 and wait > temporal.timeout-seconds.awaiting-* (default 60s). The
### Temporal workflow timer will emit PENALTY_REVOKE_COMMAND and the saga will
### transition to COMPENSATED automatically once the service comes back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass
@landlordEmail = landlord@blps.local
@landlordPass = landpass
@tenantEmail = tenant@blps.local
@tenantPass = tenantpass

### 35.1 Resolve tenant id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("tenant35_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 35.2 Landlord creates claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant35_id}},
  "title": "Saga orchestration happy path",
  "description": "Verifies PENALTY_APPLIED + PENALTY_COUNTED close the saga.",
  "claimedAmount": 200,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim35_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 35.3 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 35.4 Intake decision (no extra info)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "" }

### 35.5 Assessment with penalty grounds
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 150, "assessmentNotes": "saga e2e" }

### 35.6 Tenant agrees
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 35.7 Support decision → saga starts (currentSagaId now non-null)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 150,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "drive saga"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga35_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.test("saga started", () => {
  client.assert(response.body.currentSagaId !== null, "currentSagaId must be present after support-decision");
  client.assert(response.body.status === "PENALTY_PROCESSING", "claim must enter PENALTY_PROCESSING");
});
%}

### 35.8 Poll claim — should be PENALTY_APPLIED after PENALTY_COUNTED is consumed (~2-3s)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 35.9 Saga by id — state should be COMPLETED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga35_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 35.10 Saga by claim — same row
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim35_id}}/saga
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 35.11 Tenant penalty count incremented
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{tenant35_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 35.12 Penalty operation final state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/penalties/claim/{{claim35_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
